WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.400
“The bigger, the better!” is a phrase
you will not hear from a researcher at the

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.290
SCP Foundation.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:11.019
Larger anomalies can be a nightmare to secure,
contain, and protect, and if you’re new

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:14.280
around here, that’s kind of the Foundation’s
whole thing.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.750
But how broad is the spectrum of anomalous
size?

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.910
What deadly things come in small packages,
and what anomalous threats could lay waste

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.940
to the world in a footstep?

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.530
These are exactly the ideas we’re exploring
today with our big question: What’s the

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.530
biggest SCP?

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:34.330
Alright, now let’s set a few ground rules
before we jump headlong into the action: No

00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.550
entirely anomalous planets or alternate dimensions.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.820
This may seem like we’re excluding anomalies
like SCP-2935, O’ Death, the alternate dimension

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:49.050
where death itself has overtaken everything,
or SCP-4774, a theoretical anomalous gas giant

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.450
that’s two to four times the diameter of
Earth.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.329
But it’s a little unfair to some of the
other hard-working big SCPs by skewing the

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:58.920
results with whole universes or literal celestial
bodies.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.740
We’re also excluding shapeshifters and reality
warpers who could, theoretically, be any size

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:04.810
they like.

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.110
If you have a problem with that, we kindly
invite you to take it up with the director

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:12.180
of our complaint department: SCP-106.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:19.140
For those who haven’t now been dragged into
a pocket dimension to endure centuries of

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.870
unspeakable horrors, we’ll start with the
pipsqueaks, and work our way up to the “Oh

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.810
lawd, he comin’” stage of anomalous size.

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:31.700
Our hard-working researchers have concluded,
through rigorous study, that one of the most

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:39.310
itty bitty SCPs is undeniably SCP-008: A terrifying
prion with incredible infectivity rates that

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:44.140
effectively turns its victims into Walking
Dead-style zombies, with the only known cure

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.580
being SCP-500.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:51.050
Prions are beyond tiny, at only around 253
amino acids in length.

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:57.260
They can only be seen via an electron microscope,
and they make viruses look beefy by comparison.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:01.260
That doesn’t mean if you get infected it
won’t seriously mess up your day, to put

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.000
it extremely, extremely lightly.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:05.119
So, what’s next?

00:02:05.119 --> 00:02:11.370
We’ve got something like SCP-165, also known
as the Creeping, Hungry Sands of Tule.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.590
We know what you’re thinking.

00:02:12.590 --> 00:02:14.519
Seriously, we have the technology for that.

00:02:14.519 --> 00:02:17.779
And we know you’re thinking: “Hey, that’s
a lot of sand, what do you mean that’s only

00:02:17.779 --> 00:02:19.409
one step above a virus?”

00:02:19.409 --> 00:02:24.019
That’s because this ersatz sand is actually
made up of tiny parasitic mites only about

00:02:24.019 --> 00:02:26.879
seven hundred fifty micrometers in length.

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:29.590
But once again, don’t let their tiny size
fool you.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:32.549
They can knock you out and eat you to the
bone in minutes!

00:02:32.549 --> 00:02:36.790
But hey, at least they’ll leave bones, unlike
the nightmarish flying ant creatures coming

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.090
out of SCP-743, the chocolate fountain.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:43.359
This fountain - which is perfect for weddings,
corporate retreats, and birthday parties for

00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:47.599
your worst enemies - has the most delicious
chocolate you’ve ever tasted.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:51.540
Problem is, if you ever ingest it, millions
of these nightmarish, ant-like monsters will

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:57.180
swarm in soon after, and devour you and everyone
you love.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:02.389
The body-horror earwigs of SCP-439 are in
this same weight class, as monsters with the

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:06.360
size and general appearance of pre-existing,
non-anomalous insects.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:09.900
Except you don’t need to have a phobia of
them for these little suckers to make your

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.919
worst nightmares come true.

00:03:11.919 --> 00:03:13.870
But you know who loves bugs?

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:14.870
Birds!

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:20.579
Birds such as the common corn crake, like
SCP-2337, also known as Dr. Spanko - Though

00:03:20.579 --> 00:03:23.620
Dr. Spanko prefers bugs of the gummy variety.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:27.480
He can also literally talk you to death, with
a voice so loud and booming it’ll destroy

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:32.069
your very cells if you’re exposed to it
for too long.

00:03:32.069 --> 00:03:35.870
But his body isn’t too long, at a manageable
27–30 cm.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:41.430
He’s a similar size to other fun little
critters like SCP-131, the Eye Pods, and less

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:45.650
fun little critters, like SCP-689, the Haunter
in the Dark.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:50.159
The weight and height class above this is
one that a huge number of SCPs fall into:

00:03:50.159 --> 00:03:53.059
Roughly human, or a little above or below.

00:03:53.059 --> 00:03:57.510
The Old Man, Cain, Able, God, The Sculpture,
The Plague Doctor, The Tickle Monster, The

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.370
Swamp Woman, and Bigfoot.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:05.409
And just above that, we’ve got a number
of the SCP Heavy Hitters: SCP-096, SCP-682,

00:04:05.409 --> 00:04:12.249
Fernand the Cannibal, Cthulhu, SCP-5031, Major
Alexei Belitrov, the list goes on.

00:04:12.249 --> 00:04:15.269
But honestly, these are all still small potatoes.

00:04:15.269 --> 00:04:18.670
We’re playing with the Big Boys now, literally.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:23.420
What follows are some of the biggest SCPs
our in-house Foundation scientists could find,

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:27.150
from “Dear god, that’s huge” to so big
that your mind might boil in your head like

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.070
an egg just trying to comprehend it.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:30.470
What are we waiting for?

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.910
Let’s make like Gaston and get large!

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:37.380
First, we head to SCP-1730, the nightmarish,
interdimensional Site-13.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.730
No, we’re not going to cop out and hit you
with a building, we’re thinking more about

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:47.570
one of its scariest occupants: The giant,
bloodthirsty monster known as Leech Boy.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:52.790
Once an anomalous child named Elijah, the
abomination is now a 200-meter-long broodmother

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:56.770
with a hive mind controlling swarms of deadly
anomalous leeches.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:01.310
Even in a building literally full of terrifying
anomalous monsters, Leech Boy was able to

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:03.680
dominate with his size and power.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:10.350
Until, of course, he ran into the next entry
on this list: SCP-001 - The Gate Guardian.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:16.010
This cosmic, celestial flame warrior stands
at 700 cubits tall - Which equates to an incredible

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.730
320 meters.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.410
Over half the height of the Empire State Building!

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:24.680
If his hotter-than-the-sun greatsword doesn’t
get you, he can always just step on you, and

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.030
believe us, there will be literally nothing
left after he does so.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:29.810
It makes sense, after all.

00:05:29.810 --> 00:05:33.190
You really don’t want a pipsqueak guarding
the Gates to Paradise!

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:36.480
But what’s a servant of the Gods to an actual,
bonafide God?

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.690
Let’s take a look at another SCP-001 that
proves to be terrifyingly big: Straight from

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:47.920
the Ouroboros Cycle, SCP-001 Apotheosis, also
known as The Broken God.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:51.890
We don’t have exact numbers on the size
of this giant, metal monstrosity, largely

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:55.720
due to the fact that it kept getting bigger
and bigger as it integrated more matter into

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:57.430
its already massive body.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:02.170
The sheer scale of this utter behemoth is
best expressed in what it was capable of doing,

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:04.470
and what it took to eventually put it down.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:09.070
The monster caused considerable chaos across
all of Western Mexico, leading to the largest

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:13.300
deployment of Amnestics after the fact in
SCP Foundation history.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:17.690
In order to eventually beat the thing, they
needed to get a hand from a certain other

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.930
anomaly, but we’ll discuss that one a little
more later in the video.

00:06:20.930 --> 00:06:24.880
If you thought that a giant metal monstrosity,
nicknamed “The World Eater” by some, is

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:31.430
scary, then you’ll be quaking in your boots
at the mere thought of our next SCP: SCP-4006

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:33.100
- Massachusetts.

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:38.070
This incredibly anomalous state is afflicted
by a probabilistic anomaly known as The Veil,

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:42.100
which is meant to maintain a sense of normalcy,
and tricks people into thinking that the state

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.280
of Massachusetts has ever been occupied by
humans.

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.980
In fact, the location has been entirely devoid
of human civilization since the dawn of time,

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:53.980
we’re all just victims of the anomaly that
makes us think otherwise!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:58.080
Our next contestant isn’t wider than the
anomalous state of Massachusetts, but he’s

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:01.680
a hell of a lot taller, and way, way, way
more dangerous.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:08.770
It’s the apocalyptic monster trapped beyond
SCP-2317 - The Devourer of Worlds.

00:07:08.770 --> 00:07:12.950
This monster is likely destined to perform
an XK-Class End of the World scenario against

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.470
us, as it already has in other worlds.

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:20.900
It’s an utterly monstrous 200 kilometers
tall - Think 400 empire state buildings stacked

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:22.900
on top of each other, and then some.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:28.650
It’s a being that likely no weapon humanity,
or even the SCP Foundation, has devised will

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:31.010
be able to even slow down.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:35.100
If ever he breaks free, we can only hope that
death will come quickly…

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:38.990
But his size is nothing compared to some of
the beasts that lurk below!

00:07:38.990 --> 00:07:45.010
Take the legendary SCP-3000, the godlike underwater
being known to some as Anantashesha.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:49.730
This huge, eel-like monster is the leading
provider of amnestics for the SCP Foundation,

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:53.060
as long as they can provide it with ample
sacrifices in return.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:58.440
It’s a being so big and so deep underwater
that it’s difficult to truly know the creature’s

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:03.200
length, some estimates have put it around
or even above an incredible 900 kilometers

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.850
- That’s over twice the length of a fellow
anomaly: the state of Massachusetts.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:11.870
It’s a perfect example of some of the terrifying
things waiting underneath.

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:16.120
So what if we told you there was something
even longer, even larger than the terrifying

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:20.380
Anantashesha, lurking below us as you watch
this very video?

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:24.490
And furthermore, what if we told you that
it was super adorable, too?

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:29.290
Meet SCP-2952, also known as the Infinite
Corgi.

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:33.589
This male Pembroke Welsh Corgi measures over
30,000 kilometers in length.

00:08:33.589 --> 00:08:37.099
That’s a hell of a lot of Good Boy, where
could we possibly put it all?

00:08:37.099 --> 00:08:41.759
Well, his head and front legs protrude adorably
from the ground in Portland, Oregon, and his

00:08:41.759 --> 00:08:47.019
30,000 kilometers of corgi body place his
rear end in a rural area of Japan's Kariwa

00:08:47.019 --> 00:08:48.019
District.

00:08:48.019 --> 00:08:52.959
His body weaves under the Americas, Europe,
and much of Asia, putting the length of Anantashesha

00:08:52.959 --> 00:08:53.959
to shame.

00:08:53.959 --> 00:08:58.470
There’s a lot more to SCP-2952 than we can
really get into here, but if you want a full

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:02.560
video on the world’s longest Good Boy, sound
off about it in the comments.

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.930
And now we’re down to the big three.

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:08.920
The ones that could drive you mad even trying
to comprehend their scale.

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:12.970
Try to take it all in, if they can even fit
into your field of vision.

00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:17.589
While this next anomaly isn’t as long as
the Infinite Corgi, its sheer bulk is terrifying

00:09:17.589 --> 00:09:19.399
on a whole different level.

00:09:19.399 --> 00:09:23.029
It’s SCP-169, also known as The Leviathan.

00:09:23.029 --> 00:09:27.600
Thankfully, this incredible beast is lying
dormant underneath an archipelago, but like

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:32.240
the world’s various scary supervolcanoes,
the risk of the Leviathan someday rising and

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:37.220
causing chaos across the globe with its mere
movements is never out of the question.

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:43.139
Just in terms of sheer, raw largeness, SCP-169
is probably the biggest anomaly currently

00:09:43.139 --> 00:09:44.300
living on earth.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.740
But that doesn’t mean we’re done just
yet.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:52.499
For our next two shining examples of megalophobia-inducing
monstrosity, we need to head a little further

00:09:52.499 --> 00:09:54.360
out into the cosmos.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:10:01.120
First, to the creature sucking the life out
of the giant star that gives all of us life:

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:04.199
SCP-1682, also known as the Solar Parasite.

00:10:04.199 --> 00:10:08.249
This monster is described by personnel on
the case as a kind of cosmic tapeworm that

00:10:08.249 --> 00:10:10.720
siphons energy out of stars like our sun.

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:15.899
It’s over 28,000 kilometers long, and there’s
a good chance that it means us great harm.

00:10:15.899 --> 00:10:20.250
Just goes to show: There are no good tapeworms,
whether they’re wreaking havoc on your intestines

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:22.240
or your entire solar system.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:29.240
And now, the big daddy to end all big daddies,
the biggest SCP that isn’t a planet, dimension,

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:37.009
or portion of space: SCP-2399, an unimaginably
huge weapon of mass destruction known as A

00:10:37.009 --> 00:10:38.920
Malfunctioning Destroyer.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:43.259
This alien superweapon, sent to completely
destroy the earth, instead ended up getting

00:10:43.259 --> 00:10:48.350
stranded on Jupiter and causing a mark on
the surface known as the Great Red Eye - Which,

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:51.029
by the way, is bigger than the entirety of
planet earth.

00:10:51.029 --> 00:10:55.670
It’s currently being repaired, and if ever
it completes its goal, it will likely continue

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.019
its mission and wipe us all out.

00:10:58.019 --> 00:11:02.139
To give you an idea of just how much more
powerful this mechanized alien nightmare is

00:11:02.139 --> 00:11:08.119
compared to pretty much everything else on
this list: SCP-2399 was instrumental in defeating

00:11:08.119 --> 00:11:13.790
and eventually destroying SCP-001 Apotheosis,
the Broken God.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:18.720
Seeing as it’s currently 713,000,000 miles
away, it’s difficult to tell exactly how

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:20.899
big SCP-2399 is.

00:11:20.899 --> 00:11:26.249
But one thing is for sure: If ever you get
close enough to find out, you’re as good

00:11:26.249 --> 00:11:27.249
as dead.

00:11:27.249 --> 00:11:30.699
So, there you have it: The biggest SCPs out
there.

00:11:30.699 --> 00:11:31.930
Which was your favorite?

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:33.490
Let us know down in the comments.

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.760
Oh, and if you’re new here, be sure to subscribe.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.939
It can make a big difference.

00:11:38.939 --> 00:11:46.269
Now go check out “SCP-2935 O, Death and
More Epic SCP Stories You Can't Miss” and

00:11:46.269 --> 00:11:52.379
“SCP-002 The Living Room &amp; the Most Terrifying
SCP Rooms” for more unforgettable anomalous

00:11:52.379 --> 00:11:55.029
compilations from SCP Explained!

